- Source findings: 4-byte big-endian prefix excludes itself and counts 4-byte marked-header word + header + body; max Java Netty frame length defaults to 16 MiB including prefix. Marked header has serialization in its high byte and 24-bit length. Private header fields are code i16, language u8, version i16, opaque/flag i32, remark length i32+UTF-8, ext map length i32; map items use key length i16 and value length i32. Java private encoder narrows code/version to i16; Rust rejects out-of-range values instead of silently narrowing. JSON LanguageCode is enum name string and null/absent remark/body serialize absent or collapse on wire as Java does.
- Implemented `rocketmq-classic-remoting`, Rust command model, typed protocol header boundary and fixture-backed `ProofHeader`, JSON/private codecs, bounded incremental BytesMut frame decoder and frame encoder. Raw ext fields remain available. `ponytail:` records deliberate omission of a separate Rust fast-header path until Phase 18 measurements.
- Added Java offline fixtures for transaction, request/reply, large private-code request, ordinary and optimized Java FastCodesHeader layouts, and both serialization options for the existing eight scenarios. Live scenarios remain pending Phase 19.
- Added Rust fixture generator committed under `fixtures/remoting/rust-generated`; Maven verify invokes Java 5.5.1 decode and asserts request codes/body lengths on both Rust JSON and private-serialization frames.
